# A loop keeps an element it never writes precise

Verifies a loop that never writes `a[0]` leaves its recorded subtype in place,
so the repeated read stays statically charged as millimeters and prints `11mm`
on every iteration.

>>> source
let a: int[] = [10mm]

for (i in 0..3) {
    print(a[0] + 1mm)
}

<<< stdout
11mm
11mm
11mm

<<< stderr
